# Files that must not ship to shinyapps.io.
#
# R/gee.R is the important one. pipeline.R sources every file in R/, so
# rsconnect's dependency scan sees `rgee::` and tries to snapshot a package
# that is not installed -- which is what produced "The following required
# packages are not installed: rgee" during deployment. The app never calls a
# gee_ function; the Earth Engine backend was never wired in. Leaving the file
# out removes the dependency without changing any behaviour, because
# pipeline.R's source() loop simply finds one fewer file.
R/gee.R

# Developer scripts and docs. None are reachable from app.R.
run_demo.R
warm_cache.R
export_r_reference.R
setup.R
README.md

# Reference tables for the Python cross-check, not read by the app.
outputs/r_reference

# NOTE: cache/ is deliberately NOT ignored. It is what makes the eleven
# example fields open instantly instead of each starting a four-minute read,
# and on shinyapps.io a cold read is not viable at all. It is most of the
# bundle size and all of the demo.
#
# cdl_clips/ is likewise NOT ignored. 88 pre-clipped CDL rasters (1.7 MB) for
# the eleven demo fields, 2018-2025. Their main job is a fresh clone: they let
# a colleague run the demo library without first downloading the ~25 GB of
# national CDL, and without calling CropScape, which throttles and returns 500s.
#
# They would also carry a hosted deployment, where the national store cannot
# ship at all -- though there an uploaded boundary has no clip and no raster to
# cut one from, so it would still fall back to CropScape. On a local machine
# with the store present that case is covered and the clips are just a fast path.
#
# Regenerate with r/make_cdl_clips.R when a field or a CDL year is added.

# outputs/*.png also ships (about 3.5 MB of figures the app never reads).
# outputs/demo_library.csv is in the same directory and IS needed -- it
# supplies the crop captions on the field tiles -- so the directory cannot be
# excluded wholesale.
